## Tài liệu tham khảo

**ICT / cộng đồng (Tier 3–4 — dùng cho định nghĩa, không cho hiệu quả)**
[^S1]: WritoFinance — “Breaker Block (SMC and ICT in Forex)”: Bullish Breaker là “a bullish range or up-close candle in the most recent swing high prior to an old low being violated”. https://www.writofinance.com/breaker-block-smc-and-ict-in-forex/
[^S2]: OpoFinance — “ICT Trading: Breaker Block vs Order Block”: chuỗi “Low – High – Lower Low – Higher High”; breaker hợp lệ khi stop dưới đáy cũ bị lấy và giá phá lên swing high chứa nến breaker. https://blog.opofinance.com/en/ict-trading-breaker-block-vs-order-block/
[^S3]: El Trader Financiado — “Breaker block”: nến tăng tại swing high nơi cú giảm quét đáy bắt đầu; phân biệt với Mitigation Block bằng có/không sweep. https://www.eltraderfinanciado.com/en/blog/breaker-block
[^S4]: LuxAlgo Library — “Mitigation Block”: “Sweep means breaker, failure means mitigation block.” https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/mitigation-block/
[^S9]: TTrades (qua bản tóm tắt tự động, có thể sai sót) — “Breaker Blocks Simplified”: breaker gồm chuỗi nến up-close; Unicorn = breaker + FVG. https://videohighlight.com/v/75S4vwD4P1U
[^S10]: MQL5 blog — “Breaker Blocks: Why Most ICT Traders Draw Them Wrong”: dùng nến giảm tạo swing high bị phá (quy ước VAR-B); không có số liệu hiệu quả; tác giả bán công cụ. https://www.mql5.com/en/blogs/post/773691
[^S11]: LuxAlgo Library — “Breaker Block”: vùng = nến giảm trong nhịp thất bại (VAR-B); “marking conventions vary”. https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/breaker-block/
[^S12]: LuxAlgo Library — “Unicorn”: breaker chồng FVG; “if they do not overlap, you have two separate ideas”; không có tỷ lệ thất bại đáng tin. https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/unicorn/

**Nghiên cứu ngoài ICT (Tier 2)**
[^S5]: Osler, C. L. (2001). *Currency Orders and Exchange-Rate Dynamics: Explaining the Success of Technical Analysis*. Federal Reserve Bank of New York Staff Report No. 125 (bản tạp chí: *Journal of Finance*, 2003). https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/staff_reports/sr125.pdf
[^S6]: Chung, K., & Bellotti, A. (2021). *Evidence and Behaviour of Support and Resistance Levels in Financial Time Series*. arXiv:2101.07410. https://ideas.repec.org/p/arx/papers/2101.07410.html
[^S7]: Kavajecz, K. A., & Odders-White, E. R. (2004). Technical Analysis and Liquidity Provision. *Review of Financial Studies*, 17(4).
[^S8]: Shefrin, H., & Statman, M. (1985). The Disposition to Sell Winners Too Early and Ride Losers Too Long. *Journal of Finance*, 40(3).
[^S13]: Sullivan, R., Timmermann, A., & White, H. (1999). Data-Snooping, Technical Trading Rule Performance, and the Bootstrap. *Journal of Finance*, 54(5).
[^S14]: White, H. (2000). A Reality Check for Data Snooping. *Econometrica*, 68(5).

